1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,500
BOB: Hello, Pembroke Cycling Holidays, Bob speaking.

2
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:12,737
MARGARET: Oh hello. I've seen your advert for people to lead cycle trips.

3
00:00:12,737 --> 00:00:15,960
Are you the right person to speak to?

4
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:19,360
BOB: Yes, I am. Could I have your name, please?

5
00:00:19,360 --> 00:00:21,850
MARGARET: It's Margaret Smith.

6
00:00:21,850 --> 00:00:25,050
BOB: Are you looking for a permanent job, Margaret?

7
00:00:25,050 --> 00:00:30,053
MARGARET: No, temporary. I've got a permanent job starting in a few months' time,

8
00:00:30,053 --> 00:00:33,270
and I want to do something else until then.

9
00:00:33,270 --> 00:00:35,310
BOB: What work do you do?

10
00:00:35,310 --> 00:00:39,562
MARGARET: This will probably sound crazy - I used to be a lawyer,

11
00:00:39,562 --> 00:00:44,100
and then I made a complete career change and I'm going to be a doctor

12
00:00:44,460 --> 00:00:46,650
I've just finished my training.

13
00:00:46,650 --> 00:00:51,910
BOB: Right. And have you had any experience of leading cycle trips?

14
00:00:51,910 --> 00:00:55,288
MARGARET: Yes, I've led several bike tours in Africa.

15
00:00:55,288 --> 00:01:01,294
The trip to India that I had arranged to lead next month has now been cancelled,

16
00:01:01,294 --> 00:01:06,550
so when I saw you were advertising for tour leaders, I decided to apply.

17
00:01:06,550 --> 00:01:11,280
BOB: OK. Now we normally have two or three leaders on a trip

18
00:01:11,320 --> 00:01:13,771
depending on the size of the group.

19
00:01:13,771 --> 00:01:16,299
Some tours are for very experienced cyclists,

20
00:01:16,299 --> 00:01:19,640
but we've got a tour coming up soon in Spain

21
00:01:19,640 --> 00:01:23,520
which is proving so popular we need an additional leader.

22
00:01:23,520 --> 00:01:27,300
It's a cycling holiday for families. Would that suit you?

23
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:30,889
MARGARET: It certainly would. I enjoy working with children,

24
00:01:30,889 --> 00:01:36,870
and I probably need some more experience before I go on a really challenging trip.

25
00:01:36,870 --> 00:01:39,520
BOB: That tour includes several teenagers

26
00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:42,290
have you worked with that age group before?

27
00:01:42,290 --> 00:01:45,860
MARGARET: Yes, I'm a volunteer worker in a youth club

28
00:01:45,860 --> 00:01:49,172
where I help people to improve their cycling skills.

29
00:01:49,172 --> 00:01:53,880
Before that I helped out in a cycling club where I taught beginners.

30
00:01:53,880 --> 00:01:58,818
BOB: Well that's great. Now the trip I mentioned is just for a fortnight,

31
00:01:58,818 --> 00:02:03,340
but there might be the possibility of leading other tours after that

32
00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:05,520
Would that fit in with your plans?

33
00:02:05,520 --> 00:02:09,500
MARGARET: That'd be fine. I'll be free for five months.

34
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:13,080
My job is due to start on October the 2nd

35
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:17,460
and I'm available from May the 1st until late September.

36
00:02:17,460 --> 00:02:22,044
BOB: Good. Now is there anything I need to know about the food you eat?

37
00:02:22,044 --> 00:02:26,322
We usually have one or two people in the group who don't eat meat,

38
00:02:26,322 --> 00:02:30,600
or have some sort of food allergy, so we're always very careful about that.

39
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:35,450
MARGARET: Yes, I'm allergic to cheese. Would that be a problem?

40
00:02:35,450 --> 00:02:39,860
BOB: No, as long as we have enough notice, we can deal with that.

41
00:02:39,860 --> 00:02:41,630
MARGARET: That's great.

42
00:02:41,630 --> 00:02:47,240
MARGARET: It sounds really interesting - would you like me to fill in an application form?

43
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:51,080
BOB: Yes, please. Where should I post it to?

44
00:02:51,080 --> 00:03:03,770
MARGARET: Could you send it to 27 Arbuthnot Place-A-R-B-U-T-H-N-O-T - Place, Dumfries.

45
00:03:03,770 --> 00:03:06,650
BOB: And what's the postcode, please?

46
00:03:06,650 --> 00:03:10,560
MARGARET: DG7 4PH.

47
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:14,230
BOB: Was that P Papa or B Bravo?

48
00:03:14,230 --> 00:03:15,460
MARGARET: P Papa.

49
00:03:15,460 --> 00:03:20,798
BOB: Got that. If you could return the application form by Friday this week,

50
00:03:20,798 --> 00:03:23,880
we can interview you on Tuesday next week

51
00:03:24,060 --> 00:03:27,660
Say half past two. Would that be possible for you?

52
00:03:27,660 --> 00:03:31,640
MARGARET: Yes, it's fine. You're quite a long way from where I live

53
00:03:31,640 --> 00:03:33,820
so I'll drive, over on Monday.

54
00:03:33,820 --> 00:03:36,090
Should I bring anything to the interview?

55
00:03:36,090 --> 00:03:38,853
BOB: We'll have your application form, of course,

56
00:03:38,853 --> 00:03:42,340
but we'll need to see any certificates you've got that are relevant

57
00:03:42,660 --> 00:03:45,070
in cycling, first aid, or whatever.

58
00:03:45,070 --> 00:03:46,480
MARGARET: OK.

59
00:03:46,480 --> 00:03:52,864
BOB: And at the interview we'd like to find out about your experience of being a tour guide.

60
00:03:52,864 --> 00:03:56,410
So could you prepare a ten-minute talk about that, please?

61
00:03:56,410 --> 00:04:01,850
You don't need slides or any complicated equipment - just some notes.

62
00:04:01,850 --> 00:04:05,940
MARGARET: Right. I'll start thinking about that straightaway!

63
00:04:05,940 --> 00:04:10,108
BOB: Good. Well, we'll look forward to receiving your application form,

64
00:04:10,108 --> 00:04:13,140
and we'll contact you to confirm the interview.

65
00:04:13,140 --> 00:04:15,130
MARGARET: Thanks very much.

66
00:04:15,130 --> 00:04:17,660
BOB: Thank you, Margaret. Goodbye.

67
00:04:17,660 --> 00:04:19,650
MARGARET: Bye.
